From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/16] D7 call site: --retier schedules tier-policy rounds off
 the decode path and applies them on the engine thread

Nothing called RemoteExperts::seabraid_retier. This wires the policy (strata-ext tier_plan) to it
behind --retier, default OFF. The scheduling code lives in seabraid's strata-ext
(strata/seabraid/retier_loop.hpp), not in generate.cpp; this patch adds only the hooks, the link
and two read accessors.

DESIGN GATE
- Owner: round scheduling, the TierOp->TierWireOp conversion and the --retier* flags live in
  strata-ext retier_loop.{hpp,cpp}. tier_plan still owns what moves; RemoteExperts still owns how
  it is applied. generate.cpp gets: include, one Options member, flag parse, --help, a
  startup check+construct, one tick() at the serial --serve window boundary, and a --serve-only
  guard. All of it is #if STRATA_HAVE_SEABRAID_RETIER, defined by CMake only when the seabraid
  checkout provides the seabraid_retier target, so a build without SEABRAID_STRATA_SOURCE_DIR compiles
  none of it.
- Contract: RetierLoop::tick(usage, held, free_slots, quiescent, ApplyFn) on the engine thread.
  ApplyFn is RemoteExperts::seabraid_retier; the loop never includes remote_experts.hpp (one-way
  edge). RemoteExperts gains seabraid_held() and seabraid_free_slots(), both engine-thread only.
- Size: retier_loop.hpp 147 lines, retier_loop.cpp 215, generate.cpp +52.
- Failure: misconfiguration (bad value, empty usage with the feature on, no helper, not --serve)
  fails fast at startup, the error names --adapt-every and --adapt-swaps. A round error (planner
  error, helper refusal, fence timeout) is logged and the round skipped; serving continues and
  failed ops reach note_failed. Ops are never applied off the engine thread: tick() refuses any
  other thread, the planner thread only produces a plan.
- Checker: tests/retier_loop_test.cpp and tests/tier_plan_test.cpp in the seabraid checkout, each
  guard sabotaged once (tests/SABOTAGE.md).
- Finish line: with the flag off nothing here is constructed (no thread, no snapshot); with it on,
  one log line per round with ops proposed/applied/failed, ranker ms, fence ms, coverage.

THREAD MODEL. Engine thread: at a window boundary tick() takes a finished plan and applies it
through seabraid_retier, then (if a round is due and none is in flight) copies heat
(DriverState::usage) and the helper's residency into a single-slot mailbox. Planner thread: waits on
the mailbox, runs note_failed for the previous round, plan_tier_round (timed), converts to wire ops,
posts a plan to a second single-slot mailbox. The planner owns TierPolicyState exclusively; failures
reach it inside the next input. No shared mutable state besides the two mailboxes.

HOOK PLACEMENT. Just before adapt_tick() in the serial --serve loop: the previous window's adapt
thread was joined at the end of that iteration and the next is not started, so nothing else touches
usage or the helper's residency. The pipelined loop, --batch and generate mode have no hook;
generate mode is refused at startup, and the RetierLoop destructor prints a WARNING when it was never
ticked. With an --adapt-async job running, usage is being written, so the snapshot is skipped.

KNOBS (flags, all in --help): --retier off|on|zero-op (default off), --retier-every N windows
(128), --retier-moves N (4), --retier-margin X (1.25), --retier-cooldown N (8), --retier-ceiling X
(0.08). zero-op runs snapshot, ranker, hand-off and the log line, discards the ops and never enters
the fence (seabraid_retier refuses n=0, so the loop skips the call).

TRANSPORT LIMIT FOUND WHILE WIRING: the wire has no EVICT and a SWAP is same-layer, but the policy
emits bare EVICTs and cross-layer pairs. strata-ext now has TierPolicyConfig::same_layer_swaps
(default false; the loop forces it) so the policy returns only LOADs into free slots and same-layer
LOAD+EVICT pairs; to_wire() turns pairs into SWAPs and drops anything else, counted and logged.
On a full helper the free-slot count is 0 for good, so every applied move is a swap.

NOT VERIFIED: nothing was run on a GPU. generate.cpp, remote_experts.cpp and the loop compile with
nvcc 13.1 sm_86 (generate.cpp needs -std=c++20); HIP is not built here.
